from (values
('127.695.d.8.F',3,'Syncing a phone''s contacts to a cloud account helps to:','["delete all contacts", "remove the account", "keep the same contacts on all devices", "slow the phone"]'::jsonb,2,'Sync keeps data consistent.','original'),
('127.695.d.8.F',4,'A user''s calendar on a phone isn''t matching their laptop. A technician should check:','["the phone case", "the volume level", "the keyboard backlight", "that sync is enabled and the accounts match"]'::jsonb,3,'Sync settings control updates.','original'),
('127.695.d.8.G',3,'A phone runs very slowly and apps crash. A reasonable first step is to:','["restart the device and free up storage", "throw it away", "buy a new case", "paint it"]'::jsonb,0,'Restarts and storage cleanup solve many issues.','original'),
('127.695.d.8.G',4,'An app crashes right after a mobile OS update. A technician should check for:','["a laptop battery", "an app update compatible with the new OS", "a new screen protector", "a wired network"]'::jsonb,1,'Compatibility updates fix post-update crashes.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.A',3,'A technician is running a new wired network in an office. The cable most commonly used for Ethernet is:','["speaker wire", "coaxial for TV", "twisted-pair (Cat 6)", "extension cord"]'::jsonb,2,'Ethernet uses twisted-pair cabling.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.A',4,'To secure a wired network, a technician can disable unused switch ports and:','["leave all ports open", "label every port ''public''", "share the admin password", "use access controls on connected devices"]'::jsonb,3,'Port security limits unauthorized connections.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.B',3,'The first step to secure a new wireless router is to:','["change the default admin password and enable encryption", "leave default settings", "broadcast the password", "turn off the firewall"]'::jsonb,0,'Defaults are well known to attackers.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.B',4,'Setting a wireless network to hide its SSID by itself is:','["required by law", "a weak security measure that is easy to bypass", "the strongest protection", "unbreakable"]'::jsonb,1,'Hidden SSIDs are still discoverable.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.C',3,'Which wireless security protocol is generally the most secure?','["WEP", "open (no security)", "WPA3", "WPS only"]'::jsonb,2,'WPA3 is the newest and strongest.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.C',4,'Which security setting is outdated and easily cracked?','["WPA3", "WPA2-Enterprise", "WPA2", "WEP"]'::jsonb,3,'WEP is obsolete.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.D',3,'One computer on the network can''t reach the internet while others can. A technician should first check:','["that computer''s cable or Wi-Fi connection and IP settings", "the office lights", "the printer toner", "everyone''s passwords"]'::jsonb,0,'Isolate to the affected device.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.D',4,'If no devices on a Wi-Fi network can reach the internet, a likely cause is:','["a user''s phone case", "a problem with the router or modem", "a single laptop''s battery", "a keyboard"]'::jsonb,1,'Network-wide issues point to shared equipment.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.E',3,'A technician suspects a patch cable has a broken wire inside. A cable tester is used to:','["clean the screen", "print documents", "check a network cable for breaks or wiring faults", "measure room temperature"]'::jsonb,2,'Testers verify cable integrity.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.E',4,'To see whether a device can reach another over a network, a technician can use the:','["cls command", "copy command", "dir command", "ping command"]'::jsonb,3,'Ping tests reachability.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.F',3,'A phone and a laptop share a file over a home Wi-Fi network. They are communicating through the:','["network and a wireless router", "power cord", "USB mouse", "printer driver"]'::jsonb,0,'Devices connect through the network.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.F',4,'Two phones share a photo without a router by using a short-range wireless technology such as:','["a coaxial line", "Bluetooth", "serial cable", "fiber backbone"]'::jsonb,1,'Bluetooth supports direct device connections.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.G',3,'Cloud computing lets a company use servers and storage:','["without a network", "only on its own premises", "over the internet instead of owning them", "without any software"]'::jsonb,2,'Cloud resources are delivered online.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.G',4,'A feature of many cloud platforms that lets customers add or remove resources as needed is:','["immobility", "fragility", "isolation", "scalability"]'::jsonb,3,'Scalability fits changing demand.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.H',3,'A user cannot open a file stored in a cloud service. A technician should first check:','["the user''s sign-in, permissions and internet connection", "the keyboard keys", "the printer toner", "the monitor stand"]'::jsonb,0,'Access and connectivity are common causes.','original'),
('127.695.d.9.H',4,'A cloud virtual machine is running slowly. A technician may review its resource use and:','["replace the monitor", "increase its memory or CPU allocation", "clean the mouse", "unplug the keyboard"]'::jsonb,1,'Resizing resources can fix performance.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.A',3,'A team lists who will use a robot arm, what it must lift and where it will work. They are:','["recycling the parts", "selling the product", "identifying the elements of an engineering problem", "testing a finished product"]'::jsonb,2,'Defining users, tasks and setting frames the problem.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.A',4,'Which question best helps an engineer analyze a problem before designing a fix?','["Who can build it fastest?", "Which color looks best?", "What did it cost last year?", "What need must the solution meet, and for whom?"]'::jsonb,3,'Needs and users drive the design.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.B',3,'A programmer breaks a game idea into inputs, rules, scoring and outputs. This step is:','["analyzing the structure of a programming problem", "debugging syntax errors", "publishing the app", "compressing images"]'::jsonb,0,'Decomposition reveals a problem''s structure.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.B',4,'Splitting a large program task into smaller sub-problems helps because each piece is:','["impossible to test", "easier to understand, build and test", "hidden from the user", "guaranteed bug-free"]'::jsonb,1,'Smaller parts are manageable.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.C',3,'A client says the timer app must work offline. This statement is:','["a code comment", "a bug report", "pertinent customer information about a requirement", "a legal notice"]'::jsonb,2,'Customer statements reveal requirements.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.C',4,'Before changing an existing program for a customer, a developer should first:','["rewrite it from scratch immediately", "skip the customer meeting", "delete the old code", "read what it already does and ask what the customer needs changed"]'::jsonb,3,'Understand the current program and the need.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.D',3,'A team weighs two ways to store scores: a file or a database. They are:','["comparing alternatives to a solution", "debugging a loop", "naming variables", "drawing a logo"]'::jsonb,0,'Alternatives are compared before choosing.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.D',4,'Critical thinking when choosing between designs means judging each option by:','["which one a friend likes", "evidence and how well it meets requirements", "which one is shortest", "which one is newest"]'::jsonb,1,'Decisions rest on evidence and criteria.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.E',3,'Before choosing a sensor for a robot, a student reads its datasheet. This is:','["peer grading", "testing a prototype", "researching technical information for a decision", "a final report"]'::jsonb,2,'Datasheets give specs for choosing parts.','original'),
('127.696.d.1.E',4,'Which source is most reliable for a microcontroller''s voltage limits?','["A friend''s memory", "A random forum guess", "A product photo", "The manufacturer''s datasheet"]'::jsonb,3,'Primary documentation is most reliable.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.A',3,'Before using a hot-glue gun in the lab, a student should:','["wear eye protection and keep fingers away from the nozzle", "cut toward their hands", "remove all safety gear", "leave it plugged in unattended"]'::jsonb,0,'Basic lab safety prevents burns and cuts.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.A',4,'When cutting material with a hobby knife, the safe method is to:','["cut without a mat", "cut away from the body on a cutting mat", "hold the material in your lap", "cut toward your hand"]'::jsonb,1,'Cutting away from the body avoids injury.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.B',3,'Loose batteries and wires should be stored:','["loose in a pocket", "touching metal tools", "in labeled containers so terminals cannot short", "in direct sunlight on a bench"]'::jsonb,2,'Preventing shorts prevents fires.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.B',4,'Before changing wiring on a powered breadboard circuit, a student should:','["leave it powered", "touch both rails", "add more voltage", "disconnect the power first"]'::jsonb,3,'Unpower circuits before changing them.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.C',3,'Leftover wire scraps and dead batteries should be:','["recycled or disposed of in the proper bins", "hidden in a drawer", "thrown on the floor", "mixed with food waste"]'::jsonb,0,'Electronics need proper disposal.','original'),
('127.696.d.2.C',4,'Reusing a breadboard and jumper wires for a new project is an example of:','["avoiding testing", "conserving resources by reusing materials", "wasting resources", "ignoring safety"]'::jsonb,1,'Reuse reduces waste.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.A',3,'A project must cost under $50 and be done in two weeks. These limits are:','["bugs", "variables", "constraints", "comments"]'::jsonb,2,'Constraints are limits on a design.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.A',4,'A constraint evaluation asks whether a design:','["uses the most parts", "is the prettiest", "is the most complex", "stays within limits such as cost, time and size"]'::jsonb,3,'Designs must fit their constraints.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.B',3,'Adding a guard around spinning motor blades protects the:','["user", "compiler", "spreadsheet", "password"]'::jsonb,0,'Guards are user safety features.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.B',4,'Safety in a design should consider the system, the engineer building it and the:','["competition''s logo", "user operating it", "weather forecast", "paper supplier"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety covers system, engineer and user.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.C',3,'Copying someone''s code into a project without permission or credit raises an issue of:','["faster loading", "better efficiency", "intellectual property and attribution", "color theory"]'::jsonb,2,'Using others'' work requires permission and credit.','original'),
('127.696.d.3.C',4,'A student uses open-source code whose license requires crediting the author. They must:','["sell it secretly", "claim it as their own", "remove the license", "include the required attribution"]'::jsonb,3,'Open-source licenses have conditions.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.A',3,'A customer says, "The app should be easy for my grandmother to use." The need is:','["simplicity and ease of use", "higher cost", "more colors", "faster servers"]'::jsonb,0,'Customer words reveal needs.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.A',4,'Turning a customer''s vague wish into a specific need is done by:','["ignoring the comment", "asking clarifying questions and analyzing their answers", "building first", "guessing quietly"]'::jsonb,1,'Analysis makes needs concrete.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.B',3,'A diagram showing steps a user takes to log in and what the system does is a:','["bar graph", "periodic table", "process flow diagram", "Pugh chart"]'::jsonb,2,'Process flow diagrams map actions.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.B',4,'A process flow diagram can reveal design opportunities by showing:','["the keyboard type", "the paper color", "the programmer''s name", "where users get stuck or steps can be simplified"]'::jsonb,3,'It highlights friction points.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.C',3,'A flowchart uses a diamond shape for a:','["decision", "process step", "start point", "data store"]'::jsonb,0,'Diamonds mean yes/no decisions.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.C',4,'A flowchart for a program should be developed from:','["the final report", "the results of the process flow diagram", "random sketches", "finished code only"]'::jsonb,1,'Flowcharts translate process flows to program logic.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.D',3,'A target specifications table lists:','["random facts", "the team''s lunch plans", "measurable goals for the product", "the grading rubric"]'::jsonb,2,'Target specs are measurable.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.D',4,'Which entry belongs in a target specifications table?','["Looks nice", "Pretty good", "Fun to use", "Response time under 2 seconds"]'::jsonb,3,'Specs must be measurable.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.E',3,'A team studies two existing timer apps before building their own. They are:','["identifying similar existing solutions", "debugging", "deleting files", "encrypting data"]'::jsonb,0,'Benchmarking learns from existing products.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.E',4,'Describing the strengths and weaknesses of existing solutions helps a team to:','["copy it exactly", "find gaps their design can improve on", "ignore the customer", "avoid all research"]'::jsonb,1,'Gaps become design opportunities.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.F',3,'A functional model shows the:','["team schedule", "paint colors", "functions a product performs and how they connect", "parts'' prices"]'::jsonb,2,'Functional models map functions.','original'),
('127.696.d.4.F',4,'Building a functional model from customer needs helps generate ideas for:','["tax forms", "lunch menus", "office layouts", "user actions and product functions"]'::jsonb,3,'Models inspire designs.','original'),
('127.696.d.5.A',3,'For a quiz app, the essential user tasks are likely to include:','["starting the quiz, answering questions and viewing the score", "editing the source code", "wiring the router", "changing the compiler"]'::jsonb,0,'Essential tasks are what users must do.','original')
